<title>USA: Amgen faces competition - Barron's.</title>
<headline>Amgen faces competition - Barron's.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Amgen Inc faces growing competition in two key product segments, including a challenge from soon-to-be-public Transkaryotic Therapies, which plans to offer a product to rival Amgen's Epogen, Barron's reported.</p>
<p>Barron's columnist Alan Abelson writes in the October 14 issue that Amgen also faces problems with another of its core products, an AIDS drug known as Neupogen. Abelson said sales have slowed in Europe.</p>
<p>Transkaryotic said it is ready to begin U.S. clinical trials on GA-EPO, an anemia treatment to rival Epogen in the first half of 1997.</p>
<p>And Abelson said a more immediate threat to Epogen is the spectre of medical cost controls from Washington.  </p>
<p>No one at Amgen could not be reached for comment on Sunday.</p>
</text>
